{
  "id": "89rzql2",
  "title": "CHAPTER 22: INDIAN BUDGET",
  "order": 92,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "e9ir0uc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO INDIAN BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Constitution of India refers to the budget as the Annual Financial Statement under Article 112.",
        "The Budget is broadly divided into Revenue Budget (routine receipts and expenditures) and Capital Budget (asset creation and liability management).",
        "Revenue Receipts do not create any liability or reduce assets, whereas Capital Receipts either create liabilities or reduce government assets.",
        "Fiscal Deficit measures the total borrowing requirement of the government during a financial year.",
        "Primary Deficit shows the borrowing requirement exclusive of interest commitments on past loans."
      ],
      "id": "jtc1yzd"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Constitutional Provision",
          "value": "Article 112",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Main Components",
          "value": "2 (Revenue & Capital)",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Key Deficit Metrics",
          "value": "3 Indicators",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Financial Year Period",
          "value": "1 April - 31 March",
          "icon": "calendar"
        }
      ],
      "id": "dstch6r"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6wdq5hk",
      "content": "The Indian Budget is the most important financial document of the Government of India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ild4zq9",
      "content": "It presents the annual statement of estimated receipts and expenditures of the government for a financial year, which runs from 1st April to 31st March."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6pim5ij",
      "content": "The budget reflects:"
    },
    {
      "id": "24j6ecl",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Government’s economic policy",
        "Development priorities",
        "Fiscal position of the country",
        "Welfare orientation of the government"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m1topba",
      "content": "The Union Budget is presented every year by the Finance Minister of India in the Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "id": "n6jox9k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MEANING AND DEFINITION OF BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xgl458h",
      "content": "The word ‘Budget’ is derived from the French word ‘Bougette’, meaning a leather bag. Earlier, the Finance Minister carried financial documents in a leather bag."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "phpog0h",
      "content": "According to economists:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mscm4ih",
      "content": "<em>“The budget is an annual financial statement showing expected income and expenditure of the government.”</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ccgo4uk",
      "content": "In simple terms:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7dyup8",
      "content": "Budget = Estimated Income + Estimated Expenditure for one year"
    },
    {
      "id": "ha4m16x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "OBJECTIVES OF INDIAN BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zmycwxv",
      "content": "The main objectives of the Indian Budget are:"
    },
    {
      "id": "gpoe2sn",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Economic Growth:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "36dr499",
      "content": "To promote overall development of the economy."
    },
    {
      "id": "m92iy1t",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Reduction of Poverty:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oeyo18d",
      "content": "Through welfare schemes and subsidies."
    },
    {
      "id": "dsgjjwg",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Employment Generation:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89u3y42",
      "content": "By promoting industries and infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "id": "4v2ee8j",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Reduction of Income Inequality:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vddkebq",
      "content": "Through progressive taxation and subsidies."
    },
    {
      "id": "ee3nug3",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Price Stability:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nxx5b4c",
      "content": "To control inflation and deflation."
    },
    {
      "id": "ge76ut7",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Balanced Regional Development:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dt4nm5v",
      "content": "To reduce regional disparities."
    },
    {
      "id": "urrflum",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Efficient Allocation of Resources:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uxh0gzk",
      "content": "To use resources in the best possible manner."
    },
    {
      "id": "5gx3h1v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "COMPONENTS OF INDIAN BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kgazk9k",
      "content": "The Indian Budget consists of two major parts:"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f0xkfw",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Revenue Budget",
        "Capital Budget"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0m7crm5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "REVENUE BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eogn5qd",
      "content": "Revenue Budget includes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ecql8i",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Revenue Receipts",
        "Revenue Expenditure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2wf6juc",
      "content": "These are related to day-to-day functioning of the government."
    },
    {
      "id": "2msj70t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "REVENUE RECEIPTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7x8z076",
      "content": "Revenue receipts are those receipts which do not create any liability on the government and do not reduce government assets."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y5p8gh1",
      "content": "They are of two types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2qdq6b",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Tax Revenue",
        "Non-Tax Revenue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9bbijfq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "TAX REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o4a4xei",
      "content": "Tax revenue is the main source of income for the government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nw2zghf",
      "content": "Taxes are compulsory payments made by citizens to the government without any direct return."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gl1h06i",
      "content": "Types of Taxes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "uppo99h",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Direct Taxes",
        "Indirect Taxes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a54ri6s",
      "content": "Direct tax is paid directly by the person on whom it is imposed. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "gm9ivms",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Income Tax",
        "Corporate Tax"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k1rys2h",
      "content": "Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "awzzlm0",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Progressive in nature",
        "Burden cannot be shifted",
        "Reduces income inequality"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eebgday",
      "content": "Merits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9dw3m1",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Promotes equality",
        "Stable source of revenue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cydx7iq",
      "content": "Demerits:"
    },
    {
      "id": "rxt0ywa",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Tax evasion",
        "Discourages savings"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kg8tedl",
      "content": "Indirect tax is paid indirectly by consumers. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kmm8nr2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "GST",
        "Customs Duty"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yj7l88r",
      "content": "Features:"
    },
    {
      "id": "15jhepq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Burden can be shifted",
        "Regressive in nature",
        "Easy to collect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ob32r2",
      "content": "GST (Goods and Services Tax):"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Revenue Budget",
        "Capital Budget"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Scope",
          "Deals with routine, day-to-day government financial operations.",
          "Deals with long-term financial operations, assets, and liabilities."
        ],
        [
          "Receipt Impact",
          "Neither creates liability nor reduces assets (e.g., Taxes, Fees).",
          "Creates liability or reduces assets (e.g., Loans, Disinvestment)."
        ],
        [
          "Expenditure Impact",
          "Does not lead to asset creation (e.g., Salaries, Interest payments).",
          "Leads to creation of assets or reduction of liabilities (e.g., Infrastructure, Loan repayment)."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "lpgzyii"
    },
    {
      "id": "hehmlmq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Introduced in 2017",
        "One Nation One Tax",
        "Replaced multiple indirect taxes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7yth21x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "NON-TAX REVENUE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ipe2o3v",
      "content": "Non-tax revenue includes income earned by the government other than taxes. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "1t2ngig",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li><ul><li><ul><li>Fees</li><li>Fines and penalties</li><li>Interest receipts</li><li>Profit from public sector undertakings</li><li>Grants and donations</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li><ul><li>Fees</li><li>Fines and penalties</li><li>Interest receipts</li><li>Profit from public sector undertakings</li><li>Grants and donations</li></ul></li></ul>",
        "<ul><li>Fees</li><li>Fines and penalties</li><li>Interest receipts</li><li>Profit from public sector undertakings</li><li>Grants and donations</li></ul>",
        "Fees",
        "Fines and penalties",
        "Interest receipts",
        "Profit from public sector undertakings",
        "Grants and donations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "on7qwbj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "REVENUE EXPENDITURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1d31oj0",
      "content": "Revenue expenditure refers to expenditure that does not create assets. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "iyflcus",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Salaries of government employees",
        "Pension payments",
        "Interest on loans",
        "Subsidies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7g6fcmf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CAPITAL BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u4bc92w",
      "content": "Capital Budget includes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ohbping",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Capital Receipts",
        "Capital Expenditure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lvw79k6",
      "content": "It deals with long-term development of the economy."
    },
    {
      "id": "xus6a6w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "CAPITAL RECEIPTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v2lpfqu",
      "content": "Capital receipts are receipts that create liability or reduce assets. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "i6c3zwi",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Borrowings",
        "Disinvestment",
        "Recovery of loans"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "y0jhvqu",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "CAPITAL EXPENDITURE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c0pdbqy",
      "content": "Capital expenditure leads to creation of assets. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "83rt0j7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Construction of roads",
        "Railways",
        "Dams",
        "Infrastructure projects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "i4ibkpp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DEFICITS IN BUDGET (MOST IMPORTANT)"
    },
    {
      "id": "xq83j91",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "REVENUE DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ytk9ack",
      "content": "Revenue Deficit = Revenue Expenditure – Revenue Receipts Meaning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iil3aey",
      "content": "It indicates that the government is unable to meet its regular expenses from its income."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rgyzr2c",
      "content": "Effects:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ak7ss6h",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Negative for economy",
        "Increases debt burden",
        "Reduces future growth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ty9x0nr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FISCAL DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vwdiidw",
      "content": "Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure – (Revenue Receipts + Non-debt Capital Receipts) Meaning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 112: The term 'Budget' is not explicitly used in the Constitution; it is officially titled 'Annual Financial Statement'.",
        "Formula: Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure - Total Receipts excluding Borrowings.",
        "Formula: Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit - Interest Payments.",
        "Tax Revenue Classification: Direct taxes (e.g., Income Tax, Corporate Tax) vs. Indirect taxes (e.g., GST, Excise Duty)."
      ],
      "id": "0ufbfb7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nczf7at",
      "content": "It shows total borrowing requirement of the government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4v3xfws",
      "content": "High Fiscal Deficit leads to:"
    },
    {
      "id": "q7gzjr4",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Inflation",
        "Increase in public debt",
        "Higher interest rates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ofb8cut",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "PRIMARY DEFICIT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fc9tkhc",
      "content": "Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit – Interest Payments Meaning:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wd9txxz",
      "content": "It shows current year’s fiscal position excluding past debt."
    },
    {
      "id": "z0j41lc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "id": "lsbldad",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Balanced Budget – Income equals expenditure",
        "Surplus Budget – Income exceeds expenditure",
        "Deficit Budget – Expenditure exceeds income"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r6zk53w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ROLE OF BUDGET IN ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "m2vd8oh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Promotes economic growth",
        "Controls inflation",
        "Reduces poverty",
        "Encourages investment",
        "Maintains economic stability"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uxub8ga",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "IMPORTANCE OF INDIAN BUDGET"
    },
    {
      "id": "w4mmem0",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Shows government’s economic policy",
        "Helps in resource allocation",
        "Encourages development",
        "Ensures financial discipline",
        "Strengthens economy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prvievz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONCLUSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rzrveoo",
      "content": "The Indian Budget is a powerful instrument of economic policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qvutpdq",
      "content": "It plays a vital role in promoting growth, development, and social justice."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h35zib7",
      "content": "A well-prepared budget ensures balanced and sustainable economic development."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}